# SDDK companion `.ignore` for ripgrep / opencode tools
#
# Purpose: keep SDDK-generated paths *locally readable and searchable* by
# opencode's `grep`, `glob`, and `Read` tools even though the matching paths
# are also listed in the project's `.gitignore`.
#
# Background:
#   opencode's `grep` and `glob` are backed by ripgrep, which respects
#   `.gitignore` by default. Without this file, every SDDK artifact path
#   would be invisible to those tools, breaking phase agents that need to
#   read `sddk/{change}/verify-report.md`, `docs/ROADMAP.md`, etc.
#
#   ripgrep's `.ignore` file is a separate input that ADDS patterns. Lines
#   starting with `!` re-include a path even when it's been ignored. See:
#   https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/web/src/content/docs/tools.mdx#internals--ignore-patterns
#
# Contract (SDDK v3.3 Local-Only Artifact Policy):
#   - Paths in the project's `.gitignore`      → not pushed to remote git.
#   - Paths in this `.ignore` file (with `!`)  → kept readable by opencode
#                                                phase agents on this machine.
#   - These two facts are independent. Both must hold for SDDK to function.
#
# Ref: prompts/sdd-kernel/git-contract.md § Local-Only Artifact Policy

# Allow SDDK-generated dirs to be searched/read locally
!sddk/
!sddk/**

!openspec/changes/
!openspec/changes/**

!.atl/
!.atl/**

# Allow SDDK-generated files under docs/
!docs/ROADMAP.md
!docs/ROADMAP.local.*
!docs/adr/
!docs/adr/**
!docs/reports/
!docs/reports/**
!docs/metrics/
!docs/metrics/**

# Allow SDDK runtime state
!**/apply-checkpoint.json
!sddk-config.json
!sddk.local.*
!.sddk/
!.sddk/**
